<title>POLAND: ABN AMRO BUYS 74 PCT OF POLISH BROKERAGE.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO BUYS 74 PCT OF POLISH BROKERAGE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch bank ABN AMRO NV said on Tursday it had bought 74 percent of Polish securities house DML.</p>
<p>&quot;The acquisition is in line with ABN AMRO's strategy to build up a fully working investment bank,&quot; ABN AMRO said.</p>
<p>The Polish firm has 28 employees and deals with private investors.</p>
<p>The price of the acquisition has not been dislosed.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO has 1,670 offices in 68 countries worldwide.</p>
</text>
